course: dictionary
lesson: 6958
title: Palette: a word with many colours
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A palette is a flat board or tray that an artist uses to hold and mix paints. Context tells you which meaning is meant: if the sentence is about mixing paint, the word means the tray.
explain: Palette can also mean the set of colours used in a painting, a room, a design or a computer program. When a designer says «a palette of blues and greens», the word means the group of colours to choose from. Ask yourself: is someone holding paint, or choosing colours?
explain: Palette can even mean a range of things to choose from, such as sounds or flavours. Do not mix it up with palate, which means the sense of taste. A useful check is to swap in "range of colours" or "tray for paints" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Palette means a flat board or tray that an artist uses to mix paints.
fact: Palette can mean the set of colours in a painting, a room or a design.
fact: «A palette of blues and greens» means a group of blue and green colours to choose from.
fact: Palette can also mean a range of things to choose from, such as sounds or flavours.
fact: Palate (not palette) means the sense of taste.
exercise: «Each paint soaks up part of the light, so mixing too many paints together soaks up almost everything and gives mud; picture Mia stirring her whole palette and getting puddle-water brown.» What is the palette in this sentence? | A kind of cake | A brush with soft hairs | *A flat board or tray where Mia mixes her paints | A small pot of water
exercise: Ruby says, «Our class picked a palette of warm reds and oranges for the poster.» What does palette mean here? | A lesson about taste | A tray for stirring glue | A kind of paper | *The set of colours chosen for the poster
exercise: Which word means the sense of taste? | Palette | Plate | *Palate | Pallet
test: In a computer program, what is a colour palette? | A tool for drawing straight lines | A set of paint brushes | A file full of sounds | *The group of colours you can choose from
test: Which sentence uses palette to mean a range of things to choose from? | The screen showed a bright red button. | Mia's palette was covered in brown paint. | *The café offered a palette of flavours, from mint to mango. | The painter cleaned her palette after lunch.
exam: Using the sentence about Mia, what does mixing too many paints on a palette give? | *Mud, because the paints soak up almost all the light | Bright new colours that shine | Clear water | A rainbow
